# Companion module-base 1.13.2 preset API — implementation notes for the disguise-liveupdate preset library

Primary source used: the locally installed `@companion-module/base` **1.13.2** (`node_modules/@companion-module/base`, package.json `"version": "1.13.2"`). Host-side behaviour is quoted from the Companion **v5.0.4** tag (raw GitHub files, saved under `module-base/`). All wiki pages now redirect to companion.free; those pages were curl'd and stripped.

---

## (a) `CompanionPresetDefinitions` / `CompanionButtonPresetDefinition` — full shape

File: `node_modules/@companion-module/base/dist/module-api/preset.d.ts` (1.13.2)

```ts
export interface CompanionPresetDefinitions {
    [id: string]: CompanionButtonPresetDefinition | CompanionTextPresetDefinition | undefined;
}
export type CompanionPresetDefinition = CompanionButtonPresetDefinition | CompanionTextPresetDefinition;

export interface CompanionButtonPresetDefinition {
    /** The type of this preset */
    type: 'button';
    /** The category of this preset, for grouping */
    category: string;
    /** The name of this preset */
    name: string;
    /** The base style of this preset, this will be copied to the button */
    style: CompanionButtonStyleProps;
    /** Preview style for preset, will be used in GUI for preview */
    previewStyle?: CompanionButtonStyleProps;
    /** Options for this preset */
    options?: CompanionButtonPresetOptions;
    /** The feedbacks on the button */
    feedbacks: CompanionPresetFeedback[];
    steps: CompanionButtonStepActions[];
}
export interface CompanionTextPresetDefinition {
    type: 'text';
    category: string;
    name: string;
    /** The text to display */
    text: string;
}
export interface CompanionButtonPresetOptions {
    /** Use relative delays between the actions executing (default = false) */
    relativeDelay?: boolean;
    /** Auto-progress the current step when releasing the button (default = true) */
    stepAutoProgress?: boolean;
    /** Enable rotary actions for this button (default = false) */
    rotaryActions?: boolean;
}
export interface CompanionButtonStepActions {
    /** Name of this step */
    name?: string;
    /** The button down actions */
    down: CompanionPresetAction[];
    /** The button up actions */
    up: CompanionPresetAction[];
    rotate_left?: CompanionPresetAction[];
    rotate_right?: CompanionPresetAction[];
    [delay: number]: CompanionPresetActionsWithOptions | CompanionPresetAction[];
}
export interface CompanionPresetActionsWithOptions {
    options?: CompanionActionSetOptions;   // { runWhileHeld?: boolean }
    actions: CompanionPresetAction[];
}
export interface CompanionPresetAction {
    actionId: string;
    /** The execution delay of the action */
    delay?: number;
    options: CompanionOptionValues;
    headline?: string;
}
export interface CompanionPresetFeedback {
    feedbackId: string;
    options: CompanionOptionValues;
    /** If a boolean feedback, the style effect of the feedback */
    style?: CompanionFeedbackButtonStyleResult;     // = Partial<CompanionButtonStyleProps>
    /** If a boolean feedback, invert the value of the feedback */
    isInverted?: boolean;
    headline?: string;
}
```

Multi-step declaration: one array element per step; `steps[0]` is step 1, `steps[1]` step 2, etc. companion.free presets-1.x: "the steps are determined by positions in the steps array ... By default, each time the button is released it will shift to the next step, this can be disabled by setting `options: { stepAutoProgress: false }`". Host maps this to `stepProgression: (rawPreset.options?.stepAutoProgress ?? true) ? 'auto' : 'manual'` (`PresetsLegacy.ts:170`). If `steps` is empty the host injects one empty step (`PresetsLegacy.ts:223-229`). Step `name` and action/feedback `headline` exist since module-base 1.9.0 (CHANGELOG: "allow presets to define action/feedback headlines", "allow presets to define step names").

Rotary: set `options.rotaryActions: true` and populate `rotate_left`/`rotate_right` on each step (doc example at presets-1.x lines 190-229). Duration groups: numeric key inside a step (`2000: { options: { runWhileHeld: true }, actions: [...] }`). Valid set ids are enforced host-side by `validateActionSetId` (`shared-lib/lib/ControlId.ts:130-150`): `'down' | 'up' | 'rotate_left' | 'rotate_right'` or a number/numeric string; anything else is logged `Invalid set id` and dropped (`PresetsLegacy.ts:207-211`).

Action `delay`: with `relativeDelay` unset/false the host converts absolute delays into `internal:wait` actions (`PresetUtils.ts:convertActionsDelay`, "delay is greater than the last one, translate it to a relative delay"); with `relativeDelay: true` each `delay` is a relative wait before that action.

Serialization: `setPresetDefinitions` just spreads each definition and adds `id` from the object key; `undefined` values are skipped (`dist/module-api/base.js:251-262`):
```js
for (const [id, preset] of Object.entries(presets)) {
    if (preset) { hostPresets.push({ ...preset, id }); }
}
this.#ipcWrapper.sendWithNoCb('setPresetDefinitions', { presets: hostPresets });
```
Because this is `Object.entries`, integer-like preset ids are reordered numerically by JS before string keys — use non-numeric ids.

## (b) `CompanionButtonStyleProps` and expression-mode text

File: `dist/module-api/style.d.ts` (1.13.2) — verbatim:
```ts
export type CompanionAlignment = 'left:top' | 'center:top' | 'right:top' | 'left:center' | 'center:center' | 'right:center' | 'left:bottom' | 'center:bottom' | 'right:bottom';
export type CompanionTextSize = 'auto' | '7' | '14' | '18' | '24' | '30' | '44' | number;
export interface CompanionButtonStyleProps {
    text: string;
    /**
     * Whether the text should be treated as an expression
     */
    textExpression?: boolean;
    size: CompanionTextSize;
    color: number;
    bgcolor: number;
    alignment?: CompanionAlignment;
    pngalignment?: CompanionAlignment;
    png64?: string;
    show_topbar?: boolean;
}
```
**`textExpression?: boolean` is present in 1.13.2** (added in 1.9.0 — CHANGELOG.md line 112: "add missing `textExpression` style property"). There is no `text_expression`/`isExpression` field. The host honours it for the base style, feedback `style`, and `previewStyle` alike: `ConvertLegacyStyleToElements.ts:84` `text: style.text !== undefined ? { isExpression: !!style.textExpression, value: style.text } : undefined`; `PresetUtils.ts:117-126` defaults it to `false`.

Host conversions worth knowing (`ConvertLegacyStyleToElements.ts`): `size: 'auto'` → shrink-to-fit; numeric size is multiplied by 2.1 (topbar) / 1.667 (no topbar) into the new font units (lines 58-74); `show_topbar` true → TopBar decoration, false → Border, undefined → follow default (lines 635-644); `png64` may be raw base64 or a `data:` URL (line 626-633). Default alignment/pngalignment is `'center:center'` (`PresetUtils.ts:122-123`).

Expression functions used by the current presets exist in the host expression engine (`@companion-app/expressions@1.0.1/dist/ExpressionFunctions.js`: `toFixed`, `round`, `secondsToTimestamp`, `msToTimestamp`, `jsonpath`, `jsonparse`, `bool`).

Variable prefix in preset text is rewritten by the host to the connection's actual label — `Definitions.ts:586-593` "Clean up variable references: $(label:variable) since the name of the connection is dynamic" using `REPLACE_VARIABLE_REGEX = /\$\(([^:$)]+):([^)]+)\)/` and `allowedSet = new Set(['local'])`. So `$(liveupdate:foo)` in preset text/expressions becomes `$(<user label>:foo)`; only `$(local:...)` is preserved. Do not reference other connections' variables in preset text (they would be rewritten too).

## (c) Category ordering in the Companion UI

Companion 5.0.4 host converts 1.x categories to UI sections here — `companion/lib/Instance/Connection/PresetsLegacy.ts:61-78`:
```ts
const sortedCategories = new Set<string>(rawPresets.map((p) => p.category)).values().toArray().sort()
sortedCategories.forEach((category, i) => {
    if (BANNED_PROPS.has(category)) return
    ...
    uiPresets[category] = { id: category, name: category, order: i, description: undefined, ... }
```
So **categories are sorted alphabetically** (plain JS `.sort()`, i.e. UTF-16 code-unit order: digits < uppercase < lowercase), **not definition order**. The webui then sorts by that `order` (v5.0.4 `webui/src/Buttons/Presets/PresetsSectionsList.tsx:35` `.sort((a, b) => a.order - b.order)`). If you want a specific order, prefix categories (e.g. `1. Health`, `2. Transport`).

**Presets inside a category keep definition order** (`splitPresetsIntoGroups`, `order: currentIndex++`, lines 92-131). A `type: 'text'` preset starts a new sub-group whose heading is the text preset's `name` and whose description is its `text` (lines 93-105) — useful as an in-category divider/explanation. Category names and preset ids equal to `BANNED_PROPS` (`'__proto__'`, `'constructor'`, `'prototype'`, … from `@companion-app/expressions@1.0.1/dist/ExpressionResolve.js:3`) are dropped.

## (d) `'advanced'` feedbacks in presets and what `style` means

The type allows any `feedbackId`; `style` is documented as boolean-only: preset.d.ts "If a boolean feedback, the style effect of the feedback"; presets-1.x doc: "The style property is only valid for 'boolean' feedbacks, and defines the style change it will have."

Host behaviour in 5.0.4 (`ConvertLegacyStyleToElements.ts:335-356`):
```ts
if ('style' in fb && fb.style && (Object.keys(fb.style).length > 0 || fb.connectionId !== 'internal')) {
    // Must be boolean, translate the props as such
    ...ConvertBooleanFeedbackStyleToOverrides(parsedStyle, selectedElementIds)
} else {
    hasAnyAdvancedFeedbacks = true
    // Should be advanced, translate all properties
    overrides = CreateAdvancedFeedbackStyleOverrides(selectedElementIds, bufferElement.id, undefined)
}
```
Consequences for `liveUpdateVariable` (an `'advanced'` feedback per `src/feedbacks.ts:23`):
- **Omit `style` entirely** (as the existing presets do). Passing `style: {}` on a module feedback takes the boolean branch (because `connectionId !== 'internal'`) and yields zero overrides, so the advanced result would be ignored.
- With `style` absent the host wires every returned property (`text,size,alignment,color,pngalignment,png64,bgcolor,imageBuffer`) as overrides; our callback returns `{}` so nothing visual is overridden — exactly what we want for the subscription-carrier feedback.
- `isInverted` is carried through for any feedback (`PresetUtils.ts:106` `isInverted: exprVal(!!feedback.isInverted)`); it only matters for boolean ones.
- For boolean feedbacks (`connectionState`) **always supply `style`**; with it omitted the host takes the "advanced" branch above (see open question 2).

`'value'` feedbacks (new in 1.13) are not useful in 1.x presets: their result is only reachable through local variables, and legacy presets are converted with `localVariables: []` (`PresetsLegacy.ts:180`).

## (e) `InstanceBase.setPresetDefinitions` — signature and timing

`dist/module-api/base.d.ts:90-94`:
```ts
/**
 * Set the peset definitions for this instance
 * @param presets The preset definitions
 */
setPresetDefinitions(presets: CompanionPresetDefinitions): void;
```
Fire-and-forget (`sendWithNoCb`). Constraints from the host:
- Must be after `init` has been received: `ChildHandlerLegacy.ts:915` `if (!this.#label) throw new Error('Got call to handleSetPresetDefinitions before init was called')` — calling from the constructor fails silently module-side (host logs `setPresetDefinitions: ...`).
- Call **after** `setActionDefinitions`/`setFeedbackDefinitions`: the host validates referenced ids and logs `Presets for connection ${label} reference action definitions that do not exist` / `...feedback definitions that do not exist` (`Definitions.ts:635-643`).
- Re-calling replaces the whole set (UI gets a JSON patch, `Definitions.ts:660-662`). Label changes are handled host-side (`updateVariablePrefixesForLabel`, `Definitions.ts:521-535`), so no re-send is needed on rename.
- The module already does this in `applyConfig()` (`src/index.ts:351-354`: actions, feedbacks, variables, presets), which runs from both `init` and `configUpdated`. Calling once in `init` is sufficient unless presets depend on config.

## (f) Upgrade script types

`dist/module-api/upgrade.d.ts` (1.13.2):
```ts
export interface CompanionUpgradeContext<TConfig> {
    /** Current configuration of the module. This cannot be changed */
    readonly currentConfig: Readonly<TConfig>;
}
export interface CompanionStaticUpgradeProps<TConfig, TSecrets = undefined> {
    config: TConfig | null;
    secrets: TSecrets | null;
    actions: CompanionMigrationAction[];
    feedbacks: CompanionMigrationFeedback[];
}
export interface CompanionStaticUpgradeResult<TConfig, TSecrets = undefined> {
    updatedConfig: TConfig | null;
    updatedSecrets?: TSecrets | null;
    updatedActions: CompanionMigrationAction[];
    updatedFeedbacks: CompanionMigrationFeedback[];
}
export type CompanionStaticUpgradeScript<TConfig, TSecrets = undefined> =
    (context: CompanionUpgradeContext<TConfig>, props: CompanionStaticUpgradeProps<TConfig, TSecrets>) => CompanionStaticUpgradeResult<TConfig, TSecrets>;
export interface CompanionMigrationAction {
    readonly id: string; readonly controlId: string;
    actionId: string;
    options: OptionsObject;
}
export interface CompanionMigrationFeedback {
    readonly id: string; readonly controlId: string;
    feedbackId: string;
    options: OptionsObject;
    style?: Partial<CompanionFeedbackButtonStyleResult>;
    isInverted: boolean;
}
export declare const EmptyUpgradeScript: CompanionStaticUpgradeScript<any>;
```
Scripts are passed via `runEntrypoint(ModuleClass, upgradeScripts)` (`src/upgrades.ts` currently exports `[]`). Since 1.13.0 the host calls a separate `upgradeActionsAndFeedbacks` IPC and options arrive "in their 'raw' form, and can contain expressions" (`dist/host-api/api.d.ts`, `HostToModuleEventsV0.upgradeActionsAndFeedbacks`); companion.free warns that in upgrade scripts option values look like `valA: { isExpression: false, value: 1 }` and offers `FixupNumericOrVariablesValueToExpressions`. Docs rule: "It is very important to not remove an upgrade script once it has been defined". Presets themselves are never upgraded — buttons already dragged from a preset are upgraded as ordinary actions/feedbacks, so renaming `variableName`/`objectPath`/`propertyPath` option ids later needs a script that rewrites `feedback.options` and `action.options` keys.

## (g) Option typing inside presets and default fallback

`dist/module-api/input.d.ts:1-4`:
```ts
export type InputValue = number | string | boolean | Array<string | number>;
export interface CompanionOptionValues { [key: string]: InputValue | undefined; }
```
Presets use this same type for action and feedback `options`. **Omitted keys do not fall back to the definition's `default`.** The host copies preset options verbatim: `options: structuredClone(optionsObjectToExpressionOptions(feedback.options ?? {}, true))` (`PresetUtils.ts:105`, same for actions in `PresetInternalEntities.ts:355`). Defaults are only applied in `Definitions.ts:createEntityItem` (lines 213-222) when a user adds an entity from the UI, not for presets. companion.free: "the options should contain all of the parameters as you defined as the options." So every preset must spell out `variableName`, `objectPath`, `propertyPath`, `updateFrequency` (and `variableName`, `value` for the set actions).

Host-side quirk: `optionsObjectToExpressionOptions(..., allowExpressions=true)` passes through objects shaped `{ isExpression: boolean, value }` (`shared-lib/lib/Model/Options.ts:412-427`), so a 5.0.4 host would accept an expression-typed option from a 1.x preset, but the 1.13.2 `InputValue` type forbids it and Companion 4.x behaviour is unverified — do not rely on it.

## (h) `previewStyle` semantics

preset.d.ts: "Preview style for preset, will be used in GUI for preview". Host (`ConvertLegacyStyleToElements.ts:378-396`): `previewStyle` is parsed like a boolean-feedback style and turned into an always-true internal `check_expression` feedback (`expression: exprExpr('true')`) whose overrides are stored as `presetExtraFeedbacks`. `convertPresetToPreviewControlModel` (`Definitions.ts:367-393`) renders the preset thumbnail with `feedbacks: [...definition.model.feedbacks, ...definition.presetExtraFeedbacks]` and strips all actions; `convertPresetToControlModel` (the drop onto the grid) returns only `definition.model` — the preview overrides are **not** copied to the placed button. Use it to show a representative value (e.g. text `'FPS\n60.0'`) in the preset browser, where `$(liveupdate:…)` would otherwise render empty or `$NA`. Only text/size/alignment/color/png64/bgcolor are honoured (`ConvertBooleanFeedbackStyleToOverrides`).

## (i) module-base 1.13.2 ↔ Companion host compatibility

- Companion 5.0.4 accepts 1.13.2: `shared-lib/lib/ModuleApiVersionCheck.ts:5-18` builds `MODULE_BASE_VERSIONS = ['1.14.0','2.1.0',…]` into hyphen ranges `"${major} - ${major}.${minor}.x"`, giving `~0.6 || 1 - 1.14.x || 2 - 2.1.x || …`; 1.13.2 satisfies `1 - 1.14.x`. Modules `<2.0.0` run through `ChildHandlerLegacy` (`ApiVersions.ts:25-27` `doesModuleUseNewChildHandler = >=2.0.0-0`), with the 1.13 separate-upgrade path (`ApiVersions.ts:17-19`, `>=1.13.0-3`). `companion/package.json` pins `"@companion-module/base-old": "npm:@companion-module/base@~1.14.1"` for the legacy typings.
- Minimum host: companion.free API changelog lists "API 1.13 (Companion 4.1+)" (value feedbacks, auto-parsed textinput variables) and "API 1.14 (Companion 4.2+)"; so a 1.13.2 build needs Companion ≥ 4.1 and is verified to load on 5.0.4.
- How the version is determined: for an **unpackaged/dev** checkout Companion ignores the manifest and reads `node_modules/@companion-module/base/package.json` (`ProcessManager.ts:768-779` "When not packaged, lookup the version from the library itself"); "packaged" means no `@companion-module/base` dependency in package.json (`ModuleScanner.ts:71-79`). A `companion-module-build` package writes `manifestJson.runtime.apiVersion = frameworkPackageJson.version` (`@companion-module/tools/scripts/lib/build-util.js:95`). The module-side `runEntrypoint` only substitutes the library version when the manifest says `'0.0.0'` (`dist/entrypoint.js`: `if (apiVersion === '0.0.0') { ... apiVersion = baseJson.version }`).
- **Discrepancy with the brief:** the repo's `companion/manifest.json` currently has `"apiVersion": "1.0.0"` and `package.json` depends on `"@companion-module/base": "^1.6.3"` (installed 1.13.2). The host does not compare the registered value with its own (`ChildHandlerLegacy.ts:151-154` only uses `verificationToken`), so dev mode works, but per companion.free manifest docs `apiVersion` "should be left as 0.0.0, the build process populates with the correct value". Recommend `"apiVersion": "0.0.0"` and `"@companion-module/base": "~1.13.2"`.

---

## Practical rules for the preset library (derived from the above)

1. Every preset: `type:'button'`, `category`, `name`, full `style` (`text`, `size`, `color`, `bgcolor`), `steps: [{down:[],up:[]}]` at minimum, `feedbacks: []` at minimum.
2. Carrier feedback: `{ feedbackId:'liveUpdateVariable', options:{ variableName, objectPath, propertyPath, updateFrequency } }` with **no `style` key**. Every "set" preset repeats it.
3. Boolean feedbacks (`connectionState`) always with an explicit `style`.
4. Expression text: `style.textExpression: true` with a template literal, e.g. `` `FPS\n${toFixed($(liveupdate:fps),1)}` ``; add `previewStyle: { text: 'FPS\n60.0' }` for a readable thumbnail.
5. Categories sort alphabetically; prefix with numbers to control order. Use `type:'text'` entries as sub-headings within a category.
6. Avoid numeric/`__proto__`-like ids and category names.
7. Keep `src/upgrades.ts` growing-only; add a script if option ids are ever renamed.

