## Open questions for the lead

1. Category ordering was verified in Companion **5.0.4** (`PresetsLegacy.ts`). The 4.x host code path was not read; alphabetical sorting there is assumed, not verified.
2. Boolean preset feedback with `style` omitted: 5.0.4 takes the "advanced" override branch (`ConvertLegacyStyleToElements.ts:350-356`); whether that then applies the definition's `defaultStyle` or nothing was not traced into the renderer. Always pass `style` for boolean feedbacks.
3. Whether Companion 4.1-4.3 hosts honour `previewStyle` the same way (always-true internal feedback) is unverified; the 1.13.2 typing only says "used in GUI for preview".
4. Expression-typed option objects inside 1.x preset `options` work on the 5.0.4 host code path but are outside the 1.13.2 `InputValue` type; not recommended.
5. The manifest `apiVersion` is `1.0.0`, not `1.13.2` as stated in the brief — decide whether to reset it to `0.0.0` per docs and bump the package.json dependency range.
6. The companion.free "version compatibility table" link on the module-library page could not be located (no href in the HTML); the API-changes index (1.13 → Companion 4.1+, 1.14 → 4.2+) was used instead.
